Incident RCA – checkout_service_p95_latency_seconds > 2s for 5m
1. What All We Checked
Service Metrics

checkout_service_p95_latency_seconds – rose from 600ms → 4.5s in 15 minutes.

checkout_service_error_rate (5xx) – remained under 0.5%, indicating slowness without widespread failures.

Database Metrics (PostgreSQL RDS)

db_connections_used – 95% of max_connections limit.

pg_stat_activity – large number of queries in active state for coupons table.

Average query execution time for SELECT ... FROM coupons – 2.8s (previously ~20ms).

External Payment Gateway Metrics

payment_gateway_latency – stable at ~300ms.

No spike in errors or timeouts from gateway logs.

Infrastructure

CPU utilization on checkout service pods – ~70%, slightly elevated but not pegged.

Pod restarts – none in the last 24h.

Network latency between app pods and DB – within normal (<3ms).

Deployment History

Last deploy: v2.14.3 at 14:05 UTC (18 minutes before alert fired).

Change included promotional discount calculation requiring extra DB lookup.

2. What Seemed OK
Payment Gateway: Latency and error rates were stable → not the bottleneck.

Network: No increase in RTT between app and DB.

Infra Resources: CPU, memory, network usage all within thresholds.

Error Rate: Low, meaning requests eventually succeeded, just slowly.

3. What Did Not Seem OK
DB Connection Pool Saturation:

Active connections at 95% capacity.

Queries queueing in connection pool.

Slow Query on coupons Table:

No index on coupon_validity.

Full table scans on 15M+ row table.

Average query time jumped from 20ms → 2.8s.

Correlation with Deployment:

Issue began within 15 minutes after v2.14.3 deploy.

New feature in deploy matches the table being overloaded.

4. Final Conclusion
The spike in checkout service p95 latency was caused by a non-indexed database query introduced in v2.14.3.
The query (SELECT ... FROM coupons WHERE coupon_validity >= NOW() AND user_id = ?) caused full table scans on a large coupons table, quickly consuming almost all available DB connections.
This saturation slowed all queries to the DB, including critical payment lookups, pushing p95 latency above the 2s threshold.

5. Data Points & Metrics
Metric	Before Incident	During Incident	After Fix
checkout_service_p95_latency_seconds	0.6s	4.5s	0.5s
checkout_service_error_rate_5xx	0.2%	0.4%	0.2%
db_connections_used	70% of max	95% of max	65% of max
Avg coupons query time	20ms	2.8s	15ms
Payment gateway latency	300ms	310ms	300ms

